capability_contract_ref: Q.UI.CONTRACT.CAPABILITY.UI_SURFACE@V0111
capability_contract_hash: sha256:f784c2268b7db442229de9d7a97707e1bf3b4c666cfe37c99decf58496e56b88
runtime_contract_ref: Q.SS.STD.P0.CONTRACT.RUNTIME_CORE@V0134
fixed_skeleton_mutation_forbidden: true
extra_operation_file_forbidden_by_default: true
module_layer_forbidden: true
direct_handler_export_forbidden: true
invariants:
- Each UI Surface consumes exact UI Module artifacts plus exactly one presentation context.
- APPLICATION context may resolve only from Q.APP APPLICATION_PRESENTATION and PLATFORM context may resolve only from Q.Platform PLATFORM_WORKBENCH.
- Q.APP and Q.Platform are alternative presentation-context providers; simultaneous or dual injection into one Surface is forbidden.
- UI Surface composes but does not mutate source business semantics carried by UI Module artifacts and does not execute source Business Operations.
- Q.Theme visual semantics are not owned or selected by UI Surface; Theme binding is consumed downstream by UI Render.
- Selected presentation-context kind and exact provider ref/hash remain stable through resolve_ui_surface target realization.
- The External Provider Surface contains only the two declared UI Surface CALL interfaces and may not be expanded by code AI extraction Instance Package or P2.
- APPLICATION presentation realization uses the predeclared receiving dependency Q.UI.DEPENDENCY.APPLICATION_PRESENTATION@V0100 owned by UI_SURFACE and bound to create_ui_surface,
  with exact Q.APP APPLICATION_PRESENTATION provider Contract Interface and Operation identity; P2.Consumer may realize but not create the dependency.
- PLATFORM presentation realization uses the predeclared receiving dependency Q.UI.DEPENDENCY.PLATFORM_WORKBENCH@V0100 owned by UI_SURFACE and bound to create_ui_surface,
  with exact Q.Platform PLATFORM_WORKBENCH provider Contract Interface and Operation identity; exactly one of the two presentation dependency bindings may be selected
  for one Surface.
external_mount_requirements:
